  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:5207",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to the activation of EW-16 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N directly targets A704, which in turn is a target of palmarumycin CP18, and this pathway leads to EW-16. Additionally, Mollicellin N is also shown to target Leukocyte common antigen, which is a target of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which also targets EW-16. These findings indicate that Mollicellin N exerts its biological effects through diverse molecular mechanisms, some of which may converge on EW-16. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the molecular network in which Mollicellin N operates, with the potential for multiple independent routes to influence EW-16. The shared target of EW-16 across different pathways suggests a possible functional overlap or downstream effect, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be fully elucidated.",
